## 0. Mathematical Foundations — Statistics and Analysis

File: [`Spqr/Math/Gf.lean`](../../Spqr/Math/Gf.lean) (654 lines)

This file provides the basic mathematical knowledge required to verify
all GF(2¹⁶) functions. Every spec file in `Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Gf/`
depends (directly or transitively) on the definitions and lemmas below.

### 0a. Core Definitions

| Definition | Type | Description |
|------------|------|-------------|
| `GF216` | `abbrev` | `GaloisField 2 16` — the abstract finite field with 2¹⁶ elements (from Mathlib). |
| `natToGF2Poly` | `Nat → (ZMod 2)[X]` | Interprets a natural number's binary representation as a GF(2) polynomial. Bit `i` of `n` becomes the coefficient of `Xⁱ`. |
| `POLY_GF2` | `(ZMod 2)[X]` | The irreducible polynomial `X¹⁶ + X¹² + X³ + X + 1` (= `0x1100b`). Defines `GF(2¹⁶) ≅ (ZMod 2)[X] / (POLY_GF2)`. |
| `φ` | `(ZMod 2)[X] →+* GF216` | A chosen ring homomorphism factoring through the quotient; `φ POLY_GF2 = 0`. |
| `Nat.toGF216` | `Nat → GF216` | Composite `φ ∘ natToGF2Poly`: interprets a `u16` value as an element of `GF(2¹⁶)`. |

#### Private Definitions (Irreducibility Proof Machinery)

| Definition | Type | Description |
|------------|------|-------------|
| `gf2ModAux` | `Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat` | One step of GF(2) polynomial long-division via XOR bit-manipulation. |
| `gf2Mod` | `Nat → Nat → Nat` | GF(2) polynomial remainder: `gf2Mod a b` computes `a mod b` on natural-number encodings. |
| `gf2NoDivisorOfDeg` | `Nat → Nat → Bool` | Checks that no monic GF(2) polynomial of degree `d` divides `n`. |
| `gf2IrredCheck` | `Nat → Bool` | Computable GF(2) polynomial irreducibility check: verifies no monic polynomial of degree 1 through `n.log2 / 2` divides `n`. |

