#### 0b'. Private Helper Lemmas for the Irreducibility Proof

The following private lemmas support the proof of `POLY_GF2_irreducible`.
They implement and verify a computational trial-division strategy:
encode GF(2) polynomials as natural numbers, compute remainders via
XOR bit-manipulation (`gf2ModAux`), verify that no monic polynomial of
degree 1–8 divides `0x1100b`, and link the computation back to
`Polynomial.Irreducible` via `Monic.irreducible_iff_lt_natDegree_lt`.

| Lemma | Status | What It States |
|-------|--------|----------------|
| `gf2IrredCheck_POLY` | ✅ | Computational verification that `gf2IrredCheck 0x1100b = true`. |
| `gf2ModAux_preserves_dvd` | ✅ | Each step of `gf2ModAux` preserves the congruence class modulo `natToGF2Poly b`. |
| `gf2ModAux_log2_lt` | ✅ | The degree (log2) of the remainder is strictly less than the divisor's. |
| `natToGF2Poly_natDegree_eq_log2` | ✅ | For `b ≥ 2`, `(natToGF2Poly b).natDegree = b.log2`. |
| `natToGF2Poly_monic_of_ge_two` | ✅ | A natural number `b ≥ 2` encodes a monic GF(2) polynomial. |
| `gf2Mod_ne_zero_of_not_dvd` | ✅ | Non-zero `gf2Mod` remainder implies `natToGF2Poly b ∤ natToGF2Poly a`. |
| `natToGF2Poly_one'` | ✅ | `natToGF2Poly 1 = 1`. |
| `natToGF2Poly_pow2` | ✅ | `natToGF2Poly (2^k) = X^k`. |
| `natToGF2Poly_surj` | ✅ | Every polynomial over GF(2) is in the range of `natToGF2Poly`. |
| `monic_eq_natToGF2Poly` | ✅ | If `q` is monic with `1 ≤ q.natDegree`, then `q = natToGF2Poly b` for some `b ≥ 2`. |
| `gf2NoDivisorOfDeg_POLY` | ✅ | No monic polynomial of degree `d` (1 ≤ d ≤ 8) divides `0x1100b`. |
| `gf2_no_divisor_all` | ✅ | For all `lower < 2^d`, `gf2Mod 0x1100b (2^d + lower) ≠ 0`. |

